\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfor $i=1,…,75.$ Find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0).$" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441112 1072 #uuid "0a412ed0-e9f7-5318-a109-33611797297f" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441112 1074 "We have a population of size $N=75,$ and $p=0.8$ represents the proportion of the population with the characteristic. \n\nTherefore,\n\n- the number of population members *with* the characteristic equals \n\n$$\nNp=75(0.8)=60,\n$$\n\n- the number of population members *without* the characteristic equals \n\n$$\nN(1-p)=75(1-0.8)=15.\n$$\n\nWe select two members of the population at random. We need to find $P({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0),$ the probability that the second member does not have the characteristic given that the first member does not have the characteristic either.\n\nIf the first member does not have the characteristic, we have\n\n$\\,$ $N-1=75-1=74$ members remaining, and\n\n$\\,$ $N(1-p)-1=14$ members remaining who do not have the characteristic.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nP({X}_{2}=0|{X}_{1}=0)=\\frac{N(1-p)-1}{N-1}=\\frac{14}{74}=\\frac{7}{37}.\n$$" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441110 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1069 "q-146450" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1071 "Suppose that  $8%$ of a particular university's student population attends the law school. A random sample of $n=100$ students is taken from the population and asked which school they attend.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of students in the sample who attend the law school? Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1072 #uuid "1d5c4439-72cc-5a29-8805-27f9db8f5589" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441113 1074 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=8%=0.08,$ and $n=100.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =8%=0.08, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.08(1-0.08)}{100} \\\\  & ≈0.0007\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $4$ decimal places." 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441102 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1069 "q-146441" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1071 "A bag contains a large number of equally-sized buttons, of which $15%$ are white. A random sample of $n=18$ buttons is taken from the bag.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of white buttons in the sample? Round your answers to $3$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of buttons in the bag is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1072 #uuid "2e62b0fb-05ae-5348-8fa8-26e1b9d8b974" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441114 1074 "Suppose we have a random sample of size $n$ from a population of size $N,$ and we define the sequence of random variables ${X}_{i}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=\\{\\begin{aligned}1,\\,i\\text{th member of the sample has the characteristic}, \\\\ 0,\\,\\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, provided that $N≫n,$ we have that\n\n$$\nX={\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{X}_{i}≈B(n,p)\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is the proportion of the population that have the characteristic, and \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=np,\\,\\text{Var}[X]=np(1-p).\n$$\n\nThe sample proportion $\\overset{^}{\\,p}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{^}{\\,p}=\\overset{―}{X}=\\frac{X}{n}.\n$$\n\nUsing the properties of expectation and variance, it is straightforward to show that\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=p,\\,\\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}]=\\frac{p(1-p)}{n}.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have $p=15%=0.15,$ and $n=18.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =15%=0.15, \\\\ \\text{Var}[\\overset{^}{\\,p}] & =\\frac{0.15(1-0.15)}{18} \\\\  & ≈0.007\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1068 #edb/ref 17592186441105 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1069 "q-146449" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1071 "In a sports warehouse, a large container contains several thousand baseballs. According to a report from the manufacturer, $10%$ of these balls are defective. \n\nA random sample of size $n=20$ is taken from the container. What is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of defective balls in the sample?\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of baseballs in the box is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1072 #uuid "3d736eeb-4230-5251-a2a5-38a3eb699594" 13194139534853 17592186045417 true] [17592186441115 1074 "Suppose we have a random sample of 